      {
         "id": "SECTION_prerequisites",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><span id=\"htAmericaAbyaYalaMsg\"></span> (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "160fb48c-1711-491e-a1aa-e1257e7889af",
                     "text": "Porto-Gonçalves, Carlos Walter",
                     "page": "pp. 39-43",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2011",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "### Prerequisites\n\nThis text continues the study of the Etruscan-Roman numbers, also known as Latin numbers. Therefore, we recommend reading the previous texts about their origin (<htcite0>) and about how to write the numbers between 1 and 10 (<htcite1>) before continuing.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "886ccce8-3be8-4aba-bc86-94864e96b355",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Text or number?",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "5fc193f7-7226-4852-82d1-706a44de71ec",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "And the missing numbers?",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Introduction\n\nIn the previous texts, we learned that the Etruscan-Roman numbers, also known as Latin numbers, use only seven symbols (<htcite0>) and we learned to write, with three of them, all the numbers between 1 and 10 (<htcite1>).\n\n**Table 1** reminds us of the seven symbols and their values.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "886ccce8-3be8-4aba-bc86-94864e96b355",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Text or number?",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "5fc193f7-7226-4852-82d1-706a44de71ec",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "And the missing numbers?",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"sequenceNum\" class=\"tableTen tableTenBgBlue mesoNumTable\"><tr><th>Numerical System</th><th  colspan=\"7\">Numbers</th></tr> <tr><td>Etruscan-Roman</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">I</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">V</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">X</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">L</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">C</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">D</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">M</td></tr> <tr><td>Indo-Arabic</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">1</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">5</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">10</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">50</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">100</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">500</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">1000</td></tr> <tr><td rowspan=\"3\">Mesoamerican Vigesimal</td><td style=\"background-color: white; vertical-align: bottom;\" rowspan=\"3\"><img id=\"idt1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt1', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 1\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_1.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; vertical-align: bottom;\" rowspan=\"3\"><img id=\"idt2\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt2', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 5\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_5.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; vertical-align: bottom;\" rowspan=\"3\"><img id=\"idt3\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt3', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 10\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_10.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; vertical-align: bottom;\" rowspan=\"2\"><img id=\"idt4\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt4', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 2\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_2.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; vertical-align: bottom;\" rowspan=\"2\"><img id=\"idt6\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt6', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 5\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_5.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt8\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt8', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 1\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_1.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt11\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt11', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 2\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_2.png\" /></td></tr> <tr style=\"background-color: white;\"><td><img id=\"idt9\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt9', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 5\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_5.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt12\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt12', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 10\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_10.png\" /></td></tr> <tr style=\"background-color: white;\"><td><img id=\"idt5\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt5', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 10\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_10.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt7\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt7', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt10\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt10', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt13\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt13', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td></tr> </table> </p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 1</b>: The seven Etruscan-Roman symbols and their values.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "Notice that, to write the numbers between 1 and 10, we used only the first three symbols: I, V and X. The symbols L, C, D and M represent values greater than 10 and we have not used them yet.\n\nHow could we use these symbols to write numbers larger than 10? Let us think about it:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 1: How to use the other symbols?</b><br /><br />To write the numbers between 1 and 10, we used only the symbols I, V and X. How could we use the symbols L, C, D and M to write numbers greater than 10? What relationship do these symbols have with the three we have already used?</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_tens",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### The tens (from 10 to 99)\n\nWe already know the number 10, written with the symbol X. In this section we will learn to write every number from 10 to 99.\n\nIn the previous text, we learned a pattern to write the numbers from 1 to 9 with I, V and X: we repeat the unit I to count, the value 5 has its own symbol (V), and when a smaller symbol is placed before a larger one, it is subtracted (<htcite0>; <htcite1>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "5fc193f7-7226-4852-82d1-706a44de71ec",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "And the missing numbers?",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a372974f-4cea-4702-852d-40e70e155583",
                     "text": "Wheelock, Fredrick",
                     "page": "Chapter 15",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "The tens follow the same pattern. In the tens, the unit is the symbol X, worth 10; the middle value is L, worth 50; and the value that follows is C, worth 100. Therefore:\n- Four tens are written XL (X before L: 50 minus 10);\n- Five tens are written L;\n- Nine tens are written XC (X before C: 100 minus 10).\n\n**Table 2** shows the multiples of ten from 10 to 90.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"sequenceNum\" class=\"tableTen tableTenBgBlue mesoNumTable\"><tr><th>Numerical System</th><th  colspan=\"9\">Numbers</th></tr> <tr><td>Etruscan-Roman</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">X</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">XX</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">XXX</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">XL</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">L</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">LX</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">LXX</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">LXXX</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">XC</td></tr> <tr><td>Indo-Arabic</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">10</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">20</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">30</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">40</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">50</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">60</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">70</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">80</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">90</td></tr> <tr><td rowspan=\"2\">Mesoamerican Vigesimal</td><td style=\"background-color: white; vertical-align: bottom;\" rowspan=\"2\"><img id=\"idt14\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt14', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 10\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_10.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt15\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt15', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 1\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_1.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt17\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt17', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 1\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_1.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt19\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt19', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 2\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_2.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt21\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt21', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 2\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_2.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt23\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt23', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 3\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_3.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt25\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt25', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 3\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_3.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt27\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt27', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 4\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_4.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt29\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt29', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 4\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_4.png\" /></td></tr> <tr style=\"background-color: white;\"><td><img id=\"idt16\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt16', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt18\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt18', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 10\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_10.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt20\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt20', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt22\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt22', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 10\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_10.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt24\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt24', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt26\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt26', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 10\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_10.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt28\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt28', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt30\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt30', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 10\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_10.png\" /></td></tr> </table> </p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 2</b>: The multiples of ten from 10 to 90.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "To read a number between 10 and 99, we read the tens first and then the units, always from left to right:\n- 46 is XL (40) followed by VI (6): XLVI;\n- 73 is LXX (70) followed by III (3): LXXIII;\n- 94 is XC (90) followed by IV (4): XCIV.\n\nNotice that XCIV uses the symbol C, which is the unit of the hundreds. This prepares us for the next section.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_hundreds",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### The hundreds (from 100 to 999)\n\nTo write the numbers from 100 to 999, we follow the same pattern once more. In the hundreds, the unit is the symbol C, worth 100; the middle value is D, worth 500; and the value that follows is M, worth 1000. Therefore:\n- Four hundreds are written CD (C before D: 500 minus 100);\n- Five hundreds are written D;\n- Nine hundreds are written CM (C before M: 1000 minus 100).\n\n**Table 3** shows the multiples of one hundred from 100 to 900.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"sequenceNum\" class=\"tableTen tableTenBgBlue mesoNumTable\"><tr><th>Numerical System</th><th  colspan=\"9\">Numbers</th></tr> <tr><td>Etruscan-Roman</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">C</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">CC</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">CCC</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">CD</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">D</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">DC</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">DCC</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">DCCC</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">CM</td></tr> <tr><td>Indo-Arabic</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">100</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">200</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">300</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">400</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">500</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">600</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">700</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">800</td><td style=\"background-color: white;\">900</td></tr> <tr><td rowspan=\"3\">Mesoamerican Vigesimal</td><td style=\"background-color: white; vertical-align: bottom;\" rowspan=\"2\"><img id=\"idt31\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt31', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 5\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_5.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; vertical-align: bottom;\" rowspan=\"2\"><img id=\"idt33\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt33', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 10\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_10.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; vertical-align: bottom;\" rowspan=\"2\"><img id=\"idt35\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt35', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 15\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_15.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt37\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt37', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 1\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_1.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt40\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt40', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 1\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_1.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt43\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt43', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 1\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_1.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt46\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt46', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 1\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_1.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt49\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt49', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 2\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_2.png\" /></td><td style=\"background-color: white; border-bottom: none;\"><img id=\"idt52\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt52', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 2\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_2.png\" /></td></tr> <tr style=\"background-color: white;\"><td><img id=\"idt38\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt38', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt41\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt41', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 5\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_5.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt44\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt44', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 10\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_10.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt47\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt47', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 15\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_15.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt50\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt50', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt53\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt53', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 5\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_5.png\" /></td></tr> <tr style=\"background-color: white;\"><td><img id=\"idt32\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt32', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt34\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt34', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt36\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt36', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt39\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt39', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt42\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt42', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt45\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt45', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt48\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt48', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt51\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt51', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td><td><img id=\"idt54\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('idt54', '0%')\" alt=\"Maya numeral 0\" src=\"images/HistoryTracers/Maya_0.png\" /></td></tr> </table> </p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 3</b>: The multiples of one hundred from 100 to 900.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "To read a number between 100 and 999, we read the hundreds, then the tens and, finally, the units:\n- 149 is C (100), then XL (40) and IX (9): CXLIX;\n- 444 is CD (400), then XL (40) and IV (4): CDXLIV;\n- 999 is CM (900), then XC (90) and IX (9): CMXCIX.\n\nNotice how the same pattern of the digits from 1 to 9 repeats at every level of the decimal system: we only change the symbols used. I, V and X for the units; X, L and C for the tens; and C, D and M for the hundreds.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_thousands",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### The thousands (from 1000 to 999,999)\n\nTo go further, we need the symbol M, worth 1000, the largest of the seven symbols. We can write several thousands by repeating M: MM is 2000 and MMM is 3000. However, writing many M symbols to represent very large numbers becomes uncomfortable.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "For numbers from 1000 to 999,999, the Etruscan-Roman numbers use a bar drawn above the symbols. In the Roman abacus that we will study in the next text, we can observe how a bar above a group of symbols multiplies the value of that group by one thousand (<htcite0>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "1aacf33a-fb94-4535-a66f-3997087fa404",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Roman abacus",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
