            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 4</b>: The multiples of one thousand from 1000 to 9000. The bar multiplies the value by one thousand.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "Let us read some numbers that use this resource:\n- 1000 is I with a bar; it has the same value as M;\n- 2024 is II with a bar (2000) followed by XXIV (24); in everyday texts we usually find it written as MMXXIV;\n- 5000 is V with a bar;\n- 10,000 is X with a bar;\n- 123,456 is CXXIII with a bar (123,000) followed by CDLVI (456);\n- 999,999 is CMXCIX with a bar (999,000) followed by CMXCIX (999).",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "Whenever you find a group of symbols with a bar above it, read it in thousands; the group without a bar keeps its normal value. In this way, with the same seven symbols, we can write every number from 1 to 999,999.\n\nBefore continuing, let us reflect:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 2: A new symbol?</b><br /><br />Does drawing a bar above the symbols create a new symbol? Or is it only a sign that tells us to multiply by one thousand the value of the symbols below it?</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
